  "_meta": {
    "description": "Vehicle rating relativities. A simplified stand-in for ISO VIN-level symbol tables.",
    "method": "vehicle_factor = make_tier x body_class x age_curve. Real rating plans assign a symbol per VIN reflecting actual loss experience (repair cost, theft, liability propensity). This approximates that with make tier + body class, which captures most of the spread.",
    "known_limitation": "No trim-level or VIN-level resolution. A base Civic and a Civic Type R rate identically here; in a filed plan they would not.",
